00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:04,160
Last I heard, you were gallivanting around the world

271
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:05,650
having a grand old time.

272
00:22:05,650 --> 00:22:06,750
Gallivanting?

273
00:22:07,610 --> 00:22:09,080
That the sort of thing you start to say

274
00:22:09,090 --> 00:22:10,980
once your dick gets chopped off?

275
00:22:11,650 --> 00:22:14,570
Did the great lords of Westeros teach you words like that?

276
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:16,790
You were gone.

277
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:18,980
Yara was here.

278
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:21,960
Being ironborn. Leading ironborn.

279
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:24,490
Getting ready to bring us back to glory.

280
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:26,860
And how will she do that?

281
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:31,020
I will build the largest fleet the world has ever seen.

282
00:22:33,340 --> 00:22:34,510
Right idea,

283
00:22:34,850 --> 00:22:37,660
except I'm the one who's going to build the Iron Fleet

284
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:39,970
because I'm the one who knows how to use it.

285
00:22:40,130 --> 00:22:41,640
I've been all over the world.

286
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:44,260
I've seen more of it than all of you combined.

287
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:47,980
And across the sea there is a person

288
00:22:47,980 --> 00:22:52,110
who hates the great lords of Westeros just as much as we do.

289
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,440
Someone with a large army,

290
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:58,420
three large dragons, and no husband.

291
00:22:58,850 --> 00:23:00,650
I'm going to build that fleet

292
00:23:00,910 --> 00:23:03,350
and I'm going to gallivant right over

293
00:23:03,350 --> 00:23:05,380
and give it to Daenerys Targaryen

294
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:07,490
along with my big cock.

295
00:23:08,110 --> 00:23:09,950
You're going to seduce the Dragon Queen?

296
00:23:09,950 --> 00:23:13,390
I'm not going to seduce her. The Iron Fleet will seduce her.

297
00:23:13,390 --> 00:23:16,020
And together we're going to take the Seven Kingdoms.

298
00:23:17,310 --> 00:23:18,970
I wasn't born to be king.

299
00:23:19,850 --> 00:23:21,670
I paid the iron price

300
00:23:22,350 --> 00:23:23,900
and here I stand.

301
00:23:25,470 --> 00:23:29,360
Euron! Euron! Euron! Euron!

302
00:23:29,430 --> 00:23:33,290
Euron! Euron! Euron! Euron!

303
00:23:33,290 --> 00:23:35,490
Euron! Euron!

304
00:23:47,080 --> 00:23:48,510
May Euron, your servant,

305
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:51,610
be born again from the sea as you were.

306
00:23:52,130 --> 00:23:55,330
Bless him with salt. Bless him with stone.

307
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:57,110
Bless him with steel.

308
00:23:57,430 --> 00:24:00,360
Listen to the waves. Listen to the god.

309
00:24:00,630 --> 00:24:03,300
He is speaking to us and he says

310
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:07,590
we shall have no king but Euron Greyjoy.

311
00:24:08,590 --> 00:24:12,120
Let the sea wash your follies and your vanities away.

312
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:14,220
Let the old Euron drown.

313
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:16,880
Let his lungs fill with seawater.

314
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:25,960
Let the fish eat the scales off his eyes.

315
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:28,480
What is dead may never die,

316
00:24:28,610 --> 00:24:31,990
but rises again harder and stronger.

317
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:42,280
What is dead may never die.

318
00:25:42,310 --> 00:25:44,750
What is dead may never die.

319
00:25:59,340 --> 00:26:01,310
Where are my niece and nephew?

320
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:08,190
Let's go murder them.

321
00:26:28,740 --> 00:26:30,480
They stole our best ships.

322
00:26:32,550 --> 00:26:34,140
Won't be enough to save them.

323
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,500
Go back to your homes.

324
00:26:38,380 --> 00:26:40,510
Chop down every tree you can find.

325
00:26:40,780 --> 00:26:43,120
Quarter-saw the timber and start building.

326
00:26:43,490 --> 00:26:45,630
I want every man bending planks.

327
00:26:45,700 --> 00:26:48,280
I want every woman spinning flax for sails.

328
00:26:49,260 --> 00:26:51,050
Build me a thousand ships

329
00:26:51,690 --> 00:26:53,860
and I will give you this world.

330
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:16,150
I banished you twice.

331
00:27:17,090 --> 00:27:20,090
You came back twice.

332
00:27:23,690 --> 00:27:25,270
And you saved my life.

333
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:31,860
So I can't take you back

334
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:34,410
and I can't send you away.

335
00:27:36,750 --> 00:27:38,200
You must send me away.

336
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:53,400
Is there a cure?

337
00:27:54,500 --> 00:27:55,510
I don't know.

338
00:27:57,380 --> 00:27:58,740
How long does it take?

339
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:01,290
I don't know that either.

340
00:28:01,830 --> 00:28:04,200
But I've seen what happens when it goes far enough.

341
00:28:05,590 --> 00:28:07,480
I'll end things before that.

342
00:28:11,220 --> 00:28:12,510
I'm sorry.

343
00:28:14,270 --> 00:28:15,380
I'm so sorry.

344
00:28:15,390 --> 00:28:16,530
Don't be.

345
00:28:17,510 --> 00:28:19,960
All I've ever wanted was to serve you.

346
00:28:23,420 --> 00:28:25,750
Tyrion Lannister was right.

347
00:28:28,670 --> 00:28:29,930
I love you.

348
00:28:35,820 --> 00:28:37,340
I'll always love you.

349
00:28:42,310 --> 00:28:43,710
Good-bye, Khaleesi.

350
00:28:49,670 --> 00:28:51,870
Do not walk away from your queen,

351
00:28:51,870 --> 00:28:53,350
Jorah the Andal.

352
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:58,020
You have not been dismissed.

353
00:29:00,190 --> 00:29:01,990
You pledged yourself to me.

354
00:29:02,690 --> 00:29:05,970
You swore to obey my commands for the rest of your life.

355
00:29:07,630 --> 00:29:09,880
Well, I command you to find the cure

356
00:29:11,510 --> 00:29:13,550
wherever it is in this world.

357
00:29:16,370 --> 00:29:18,840
I command you to heal yourself

358
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:21,870
and then return to me.

359
00:29:25,010 --> 00:29:27,190
When I take the Seven Kingdoms,

360
00:29:28,220 --> 00:29:30,110
I need you by my side.

361
00:30:09,450 --> 00:30:13,000
In the last fortnight since our pact with the Masters,

362
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,160
how many killings have been carried out by the Sons of the Harpy?

363
00:30:16,540 --> 00:30:17,650
None.

364
00:30:17,690 --> 00:30:20,930
And how many Masters have been butchered by the free men?

365
00:30:20,930 --> 00:30:23,520
Two, but that was the day of the pact.

366
00:30:23,520 --> 00:30:25,060
Since then, nothing.

367
00:30:25,060 --> 00:30:28,550
So it's safe to say that a fragile peace has taken hold.

368
00:30:28,550 --> 00:30:29,700
For now.

369
00:30:29,700 --> 00:30:31,940
For now is the best we get in our profession.

370
00:30:31,940 --> 00:30:33,150
It's not enough.

371
00:30:33,150 --> 00:30:35,150
Considering the city was on the brink of civil war,

372
00:30:35,150 --> 00:30:36,940
I'd say it's a good start.

373
00:30:37,180 --> 00:30:39,410
It's not enough for Meereen to have peace.

374
00:30:39,810 --> 00:30:42,670
They need to know Daenerys is responsible for it.

375
00:30:42,700 --> 00:30:45,100
The Sons of the Harpy have a good story.

376
00:30:45,110 --> 00:30:47,400
Resist the foreign invaders.

377
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:49,700
Our queen has an even better story.

378
00:30:49,700 --> 00:30:54,700
Mother of Dragons, Breaker of Chains and all that.

379
00:30:54,830 --> 00:30:56,990
The people know who brought them freedom.

380
00:30:56,990 --> 00:30:59,460
Yes, but do they know who brought them security?

381
00:30:59,620 --> 00:31:01,850
Who brought about an end to the violence?

382
00:31:01,850 --> 00:31:04,420
We need someone the people trust,

383
00:31:04,420 --> 00:31:07,900
someone they know cannot be bought or influenced.

384
00:31:07,900 --> 00:31:11,000
Sounds like quite the hero. Where would we find him?

385
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:13,150
Who said anything about "Him"?

386
00:31:40,010 --> 00:31:42,600
That's about the extent of my Valyrian.

387
00:31:48,850 --> 00:31:51,150
Thank you for travelling all this way.

388
00:31:51,670 --> 00:31:55,350
I know from personal experience how uncomfortable the journey can be.

389
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:03,440
The truth is we need your help.

390
00:32:03,590 --> 00:32:06,610
We had hoped that we could somehow persuade you to--

391
00:32:06,610 --> 00:32:08,500
You don't need to persuade me.

392
00:32:08,680 --> 00:32:10,370
I came to help.

393
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:13,900
Daenerys Stormborn is the one who was promised.

394
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:17,580
From the fire she was reborn to remake the world.

395
00:32:18,260 --> 00:32:19,390
Yes.

396
00:32:20,070 --> 00:32:22,130
She has freed the slaves from their chains

397
00:32:22,130 --> 00:32:24,840
and crucified the Masters for their sins.

398
00:32:25,810 --> 00:32:27,280
She did indeed.

399
00:32:27,460 --> 00:32:30,310
Her dragons are fire made flesh,

400
00:32:30,540 --> 00:32:32,770
a gift from the Lord of Light.

401
00:32:32,780 --> 00:32:35,620
But you heard all of this before, haven't you?

402
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:38,010
On the Long Bridge of Volantis.

403
00:32:40,140 --> 00:32:43,650
The dragons will purify nonbelievers by the thousands,

404
00:32:43,650 --> 00:32:46,320
burning their sins and flesh away.

405
00:32:46,810 --> 00:32:50,790
Ideally we'd avoid purifying too many nonbelievers.

406
00:32:51,140 --> 00:32:54,260
The Mother of Dragons has followers of many different faiths.

407
00:32:54,260 --> 00:32:57,180
You want your queen to be worshipped and obeyed.

408
00:32:57,520 --> 00:33:00,070
And while she's gone, you want her advisors

409
00:33:00,070 --> 00:33:02,390
to be worshipped and obeyed.

410
00:33:02,970 --> 00:33:04,840
I'd settle for obeyed.

411
00:33:05,310 --> 00:33:08,140
I will summon my most eloquent priests.

412
00:33:08,490 --> 00:33:10,640
They will spread the word.

413
00:33:11,210 --> 00:33:14,810
Daenerys has been sent to lead the people against the darkness

414
00:33:14,810 --> 00:33:19,100
in this war and in the great war still to come.

415
00:33:19,100 --> 00:33:20,520
That sounds most excellent.

416
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:23,690
A man named Stannis Baratheon was anointed

417
00:33:23,690 --> 00:33:26,540
as the chosen one by one of your priestesses.

418
00:33:26,580 --> 00:33:29,330
He, too, had a glorious destiny.

419
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:32,660
He attacked King's Landing and was soundly defeated

420
00:33:32,660 --> 00:33:34,970
by the man standing beside me.

421
00:33:34,970 --> 00:33:37,550
Last I had heard, he had been defeated again,

422
00:33:37,550 --> 00:33:41,970
this time at Winterfell and this time for good.

423
00:33:41,970 --> 00:33:43,310
We'd be most grateful for

424
00:33:43,310 --> 00:33:44,970
any support you could provide the queen.

425
00:33:44,980 --> 00:33:48,440
I suppose it's hard for a fanatic to admit a mistake.

426
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:51,550
Isn't that the whole point of being a fanatic?

427
00:33:51,610 --> 00:33:53,980
You're always right.

428
00:33:53,990 --> 00:33:56,800
Everything is the Lord's will.

429
00:33:57,830 --> 00:33:59,820
Everything is the Lord's will.

430
00:34:00,670 --> 00:34:03,390
But men and women make mistakes.

431
00:34:03,540 --> 00:34:05,770
Even honest servants of the Lord.

432
00:34:05,770 --> 00:34:09,220
And you, an honest servant of the Lord,

433
00:34:09,580 --> 00:34:12,030
why should I trust you to know any more

434
00:34:12,030 --> 00:34:14,200
than the priestess who counseled Stannis?

435
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:16,800
My friend has a healthy skepticism of religion,

436
00:34:17,090 --> 00:34:19,920
but we are all loyal supporters of the queen.

437
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:29,330
Everyone is what they are and where they are for a reason.

438
00:34:31,100 --> 00:34:34,110
Terrible things happen for a reason.

439
00:34:34,810 --> 00:34:38,230
Take what happened to you, Lord Varys, when you were a child.

440
00:34:39,340 --> 00:34:43,550
If not for your mutilation at the hand of a second-rate sorcerer,

441
00:34:43,550 --> 00:34:46,460
you wouldn't be here helping the Lord's Chosen

442
00:34:46,460 --> 00:34:48,720
bring his light into the world.

443
00:34:49,940 --> 00:34:52,600
Knowledge has made you powerful.

444
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:56,760
But there's still so much you don't know.

445
00:34:58,600 --> 00:35:01,340
Do you remember what you heard that night

446
00:35:01,830 --> 00:35:05,250
when the sorcerer tossed your parts in the fire?

447
00:35:07,180 --> 00:35:10,910
You heard a voice call out from the flames. Do you remember?

448
00:35:13,260 --> 00:35:15,710
Should I tell you what the voice said?

449
00:35:17,170 --> 00:35:20,930
Should I tell you the name of the one who spoke?

450
00:35:30,550 --> 00:35:32,460
We serve the same queen.

451
00:35:32,980 --> 00:35:35,020
If you are her true friend,

452
00:35:35,020 --> 00:35:37,490
you have nothing to fear from me.

453
00:39:12,660 --> 00:39:14,780
He saw me, the Night King!

454
00:39:14,780 --> 00:39:16,990
- He saw me! - He touched you.

455
00:39:18,640 --> 00:39:20,490
I don't know. He was close, but...

456
00:39:20,490 --> 00:39:22,090
He touched you.

457
00:39:24,690 --> 00:39:27,000
He knows you are here. He'll come for you.

458
00:39:27,430 --> 00:39:28,970
But he can't get in.

459
00:39:29,040 --> 00:39:32,330
He can now. His mark is on you.

460
00:39:32,460 --> 00:39:34,490
You must leave, all of you.

461
00:39:38,710 --> 00:39:40,370
Come on, Hodor. Help me with the sledge.

462
00:39:40,370 --> 00:39:41,390
Hodor.

463
00:39:42,400 --> 00:39:44,410
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

464
00:39:44,410 --> 00:39:47,510
- The time has come. - The time for what?

465
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:50,440
For you to become me.

466
00:39:51,580 --> 00:39:54,520
But am I ready?

467
00:39:55,690 --> 00:39:56,850
No.

468
00:39:59,110 --> 00:40:01,230
We can't defend the north from the walkers

469
00:40:01,230 --> 00:40:03,270
and the south from the Boltons.

470
00:40:03,280 --> 00:40:05,110
If we want to survive, we need Winterfell

471
00:40:05,120 --> 00:40:07,500
and to take Winterfell, we need more men.

472
00:40:11,270 --> 00:40:14,110
Aside from the Starks and the Boltons,

473
00:40:14,110 --> 00:40:16,680
the most powerful houses in the North

474
00:40:16,870 --> 00:40:20,400
are the Umbers, the Karstarks, and the Manderlys.

475
00:40:20,770 --> 00:40:23,460
The Umbers and the Karstarks

476
00:40:23,580 --> 00:40:25,740
have already declared for the Boltons,

477
00:40:25,740 --> 00:40:27,150
so we're not doing so well there.

478
00:40:27,150 --> 00:40:30,280
The Umbers gave Rickon to our enemies. They can hang.

479
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:32,330
But the Karstarks declared for Ramsay

480
00:40:32,330 --> 00:40:35,150
without knowing they had another choice.

481
00:40:35,830 --> 00:40:37,280
I beg your pardon, my lady,

482
00:40:37,280 --> 00:40:40,570
but they know that a Stark beheaded their father.

483
00:40:40,570 --> 00:40:42,600
I don't think we can count on them either.

484
00:40:44,300 --> 00:40:46,850
How well do you know the North, Ser Davos?

485
00:40:46,920 --> 00:40:48,480
Precious little, my lady.

486
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:51,040
My father always said Northerners are different.

487
00:40:51,050 --> 00:40:54,530
More loyal, more suspicious of outsiders.

488
00:40:54,530 --> 00:40:56,220
They may well be loyal,

489
00:40:56,220 --> 00:40:58,560
but how many rose up against the Boltons

490
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:00,370
when they betrayed your family?

491
00:41:02,210 --> 00:41:05,070
I may not know the North, but I know men.

492
00:41:05,570 --> 00:41:07,750
They're more or less the same in any corner of the world

493
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:10,700
and even the bravest of them don't want to see

494
00:41:10,700 --> 00:41:14,600
their wives and children skinned for a lost cause.

495
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:17,650
If Jon's going to convince them to fight alongside him,

496
00:41:17,650 --> 00:41:19,940
they need to believe it's a fight they can win.

497
00:41:19,940 --> 00:41:22,210
There are more than three other houses in the North...

498
00:41:22,210 --> 00:41:24,970
Glover, Mormont, Cerwyn,

499
00:41:25,120 --> 00:41:26,860
Mazin, Hornwood.

500
00:41:26,860 --> 00:41:30,480
Two dozen more. Together they equal all the others.

501
00:41:30,570 --> 00:41:32,840
We can start small and build.

502
00:41:33,040 --> 00:41:34,960
The North remembers.

503
00:41:35,190 --> 00:41:36,650
They remember the Stark name.

504
00:41:36,650 --> 00:41:38,580
People will still risk everything for it,

505
00:41:38,580 --> 00:41:41,090
from White Harbor to Ramsay's own door.

506
00:41:41,090 --> 00:41:42,680
I don't doubt it.

507
00:41:43,510 --> 00:41:45,460
But Jon doesn't have the Stark name.

508
00:41:45,460 --> 00:41:47,120
No, but I do.

509
00:41:50,880 --> 00:41:53,010
Jon is every bit as much Ned Stark's son

510
00:41:53,010 --> 00:41:55,080
as Ramsay is Roose Bolton's.

511
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:57,180
And there are also the Tullys. They're not Northern,

512
00:41:57,180 --> 00:42:00,150
but they will back us against the Boltons without question.

513
00:42:00,150 --> 00:42:02,040
I didn't know the Tullys still had an army.

514
00:42:02,040 --> 00:42:05,190
My uncle the Blackfish has reformed it and retaken Riverrun.

515
00:42:06,090 --> 00:42:07,160
How do you know that?

516
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:11,590
Ramsay received a raven before I escaped Winterfell.

517
00:42:13,720 --> 00:42:14,730
That's good.

518
00:42:15,670 --> 00:42:17,100
The Blackfish is a legend.

519
00:42:17,260 --> 00:42:19,120
His support would mean a great deal.

520
00:42:20,230 --> 00:42:23,090
Stark, Tully, a few more houses,

521
00:42:23,490 --> 00:42:25,520
almost starts to look like a winning side.

522
00:42:27,870 --> 00:42:29,870
I've sworn to protect you, my lady.

523
00:42:29,870 --> 00:42:31,810
You heard them. We need more men

524
00:42:31,810 --> 00:42:33,700
and my uncle has an army.

525
00:42:33,700 --> 00:42:35,580
We can send the Blackfish a raven.

526
00:42:35,580 --> 00:42:37,410
Can't risk Ramsay intercepting it.

527
00:42:37,410 --> 00:42:38,500
It has to be you.

528
00:42:39,260 --> 00:42:41,600
Ride for Riverrun. My uncle will talk to you

529
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:43,330
and you'll know how to talk to him.

530
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:47,280
What is it?

531
00:42:49,350 --> 00:42:51,380
I don't like leaving you here alone.

532
00:42:51,450 --> 00:42:52,380
With Jon?

533
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:55,170
Not him. He seems trustworthy.

534
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:57,500
A bit brooding, perhaps.

535
00:42:57,580 --> 00:42:59,730
I suppose that's understandable, considering.

536
00:43:01,350 --> 00:43:02,540
The others, though.

537
00:43:05,490 --> 00:43:08,990
Davos and the Red Woman helped a man murder his own brother

538
00:43:09,500 --> 00:43:11,070
with bloodmagic.

539
00:43:11,110 --> 00:43:13,660
And when Stannis paid for his crime, where were they?

540
00:43:13,820 --> 00:43:16,980
Already out looking for a leader with better prospects.

541
00:43:18,090 --> 00:43:20,160
And that wildling fellow with the beard--

542
00:43:20,170 --> 00:43:23,080
Jon isn't Tormund. Jon isn't Davos,

543
00:43:23,080 --> 00:43:25,070
the Red Woman or Stannis for that matter.

544
00:43:25,080 --> 00:43:25,870
Jon is Jon.

545
00:43:26,940 --> 00:43:29,950
He's my brother. He'll keep me safe. I trust him.

546
00:43:33,280 --> 00:43:34,490
Then why did you lie to him

547
00:43:34,490 --> 00:43:36,910
when he asked you how you learned about Riverrun?

548
00:43:46,200 --> 00:43:47,240
New dress?

549
00:43:48,410 --> 00:43:50,230
I made it myself. Do you like it?

550
00:43:50,460 --> 00:43:53,640
Yeah, it's-- I like the wolf bit.

551
00:43:54,860 --> 00:43:59,070
Good, because I made this for you.

552
00:44:01,610 --> 00:44:03,690
I made it like the one Father used to wear.

553
00:44:04,920 --> 00:44:06,550
As near as I can remember.

554
00:44:08,940 --> 00:44:10,290
Thank you, Sansa.

555
00:44:10,690 --> 00:44:11,690
You're welcome.

556
00:44:32,590 --> 00:44:34,260
Don't knock it down while I'm gone.

557
00:44:34,720 --> 00:44:35,990
I'll do my best.

558
00:44:42,600 --> 00:44:43,470
Good luck.

559
00:45:15,730 --> 00:45:17,660
Should we close the gate, Lord Commander?

560
00:45:18,080 --> 00:45:19,740
I'm not the Lord Comman--

561
00:45:24,890 --> 00:45:28,860
yeah, ahem, close the bloody gate.

562
00:45:40,960 --> 00:45:42,480
We can go home now, Hodor.

563
00:45:43,330 --> 00:45:45,250
Well, maybe not home home,

564
00:45:45,250 --> 00:45:47,420
but somewhere that isn't a cave.

565
00:45:48,210 --> 00:45:49,040
Hodor.

566
00:45:49,100 --> 00:45:50,790
Eat something that isn't moss.

567
00:45:53,560 --> 00:45:56,050
I want an egg. How do you like 'em?

568
00:45:56,370 --> 00:45:58,900
Boiled? Fried up with some butter?

569
00:45:59,390 --> 00:46:00,240
Hodor.

570
00:46:01,320 --> 00:46:04,070
With a rasher of bacon and some blood sausage.

571
00:46:04,070 --> 00:46:04,880
Hodor.

572
00:47:05,720 --> 00:47:07,630
Get Bran and run!

573
00:47:20,150 --> 00:47:22,140
Bran. Bran, wake up.

574
00:47:22,480 --> 00:47:25,050
- Bran. - Hodor. Hodor.

575
00:47:25,230 --> 00:47:26,610
Bran, wake up.

576
00:47:36,890 --> 00:47:39,290
- Gods keep you on the kingsroad. - Take it easy.

577
00:47:39,430 --> 00:47:40,500
Watch yourself.

578
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:45,110
Hodor.

579
00:47:45,120 --> 00:47:47,280
Hodor. Hodor.

580
00:47:48,480 --> 00:47:49,350
Help me!

581
00:48:09,360 --> 00:48:10,100
Go!

582
00:48:11,330 --> 00:48:12,140
Go!

583
00:49:00,370 --> 00:49:02,280
Remember that you are a Stark.

584
00:49:02,570 --> 00:49:04,980
Comport yourself with dignity at the Vale

585
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:07,190
and try to stay out of fights.

586
00:49:07,190 --> 00:49:08,230
Yes, Father.

587
00:49:10,860 --> 00:49:13,890
But if you have to fight, win.

588
00:49:16,010 --> 00:49:18,070
Bran! Bran, wake up!

589
00:49:30,300 --> 00:49:33,320
Bran! Bran! Bran, wake up.

590
00:49:33,320 --> 00:49:35,680
- Bran! Bran, wake up! - Hodor. Hodor.

591
00:49:42,280 --> 00:49:43,350
You have to wake up.

592
00:49:43,440 --> 00:49:45,600
- We need Hodor. - Hodor. Hodor.

593
00:49:45,610 --> 00:49:46,960
Bran, we need Hodor.

594
00:49:47,330 --> 00:49:49,780
Bran, you have to wake up. We need Hodor.

595
00:49:52,580 --> 00:49:54,360
Hodor. Hodor.

596
00:50:03,040 --> 00:50:04,740
Bran, we're all going to die!

597
00:50:04,930 --> 00:50:06,020
Bran, wake up!

598
00:50:06,450 --> 00:50:09,310
We're all going to die! Bran! Bran!

599
00:50:09,950 --> 00:50:11,840
Bran, you have to wake up. We need Hodor.

600
00:50:11,840 --> 00:50:13,450
Hodor. Hodor.

601
00:50:13,450 --> 00:50:14,860
Warg into Hodor now!

602
00:50:15,710 --> 00:50:17,890
Bran, wake up. We need Hodor.

603
00:50:18,430 --> 00:50:21,370
We need Hodor. Warg into Hodor now! Now!

604
00:50:21,420 --> 00:50:23,340
Listen to your friend, Brandon.

605
00:50:25,990 --> 00:50:27,350
Hodor. Hodor.

606
00:50:27,520 --> 00:50:28,960
Hodor. Hodor.

607
00:50:28,960 --> 00:50:30,060
Hodor. Hodor.

608
00:51:05,770 --> 00:51:07,670
- Summer! - Go.

609
00:51:08,680 --> 00:51:09,490
Go!

610
00:51:47,840 --> 00:51:49,580
The time has come.

611
00:51:52,130 --> 00:51:53,490
Leave me.

612
00:52:20,150 --> 00:52:22,280
- What are you doing? - Go!

613
00:53:11,150 --> 00:53:12,400
Hodor, hurry!

614
00:53:13,260 --> 00:53:14,090
Hodor!

615
00:53:33,290 --> 00:53:34,540
Hold the door!

616
00:53:35,830 --> 00:53:37,010
Hold the door!

617
00:53:41,300 --> 00:53:42,720
Hold the door!

618
00:53:45,360 --> 00:53:46,630
Hold the door!

619
00:53:56,060 --> 00:53:57,290
Hold the door!

620
00:54:04,450 --> 00:54:05,880
- Hold the door! - Wylis!

621
00:54:06,710 --> 00:54:07,770
What's the matter?

622
00:54:07,960 --> 00:54:10,380
- Hold the door! - Come on, son.

623
00:54:10,850 --> 00:54:12,730
Hold the door!

624
00:54:18,430 --> 00:54:22,320
Hold the door! Hold the door!

625
00:54:22,410 --> 00:54:25,380
Hold the door! Hold the door!

626
00:54:25,930 --> 00:54:27,540
Hold the door!

627
00:54:28,140 --> 00:54:29,790
Hold the door!

628
00:54:57,410 --> 00:55:00,170
Hold the door! Hold the door!

629
00:55:00,170 --> 00:55:02,830
Hold the door! Hold the door!

630
00:55:02,830 --> 00:55:05,600
Hold the door! Hold the door!

631
00:55:05,600 --> 00:55:08,260
Hold the door! Hold the door!

632
00:55:08,260 --> 00:55:10,960
Hold the door! Hold door!

633
00:55:10,960 --> 00:55:13,850
Hold door! Hold the door!

634
00:55:13,850 --> 00:55:18,110
Hold the door! Hold door! Hold door!

635
00:55:18,110 --> 00:55:20,740
Hold door! Hodor!

636
00:55:20,790 --> 00:55:23,270
Hodor! Hodor!

637
00:55:23,620 --> 00:55:26,140
Hodor! Hodor!

638
00:55:26,250 --> 00:55:27,400
Hodor!

